es/2026/09/0047235683_10.jpg";s:6:"medium";s:5:"image";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:40:"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/";a:1:{s:7:"encoded";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:19791:"<h2 id="top-pick">Top Pick</h2><h3 id="dreadnought-%E2%80%93-wars-of-spirit-wards-of-light-progressive-post-metal">Dreadnought &#x2013; <em>Wars of Spirit // Wards of Light </em>(progressive post-metal) </h3><h3 id></h3><img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/09/0047235683_10.jpg" alt="Release Roundup: 9/11/26"><p>Like <a href="https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/09/09/dreadnought-wars-of-spirit-wards-of-light/" rel="noreferrer">Eden said</a>, <em>Wars of Spirit // Wards of Light</em> is a more direct, yet still expansive album for <strong>Dreadnought,</strong> that blends the bassy, post-metal rumble of previous benchmark <em>Emergence </em>(2019) with the expansive, progressive soundscapes of their other, perhaps more progressive material. The way it balances all these elements is truly impressive, painting a lush soniscape that is at once oppressive and inviting, and the perfect backdrop for Kelly Schilling&apos;s <strong>Kate Bush</strong>-esque wails, which are themselves as equally unhinged-sounding as they are controlled.</p><p>This band might not seem like my usual cup of tea, but Dreadnought have always been exceptions to whatever rules you want to throw at them. when something is done with such obvious passion and mastery it&apos;s impossible to resist, and <em>Wars of Spirit // Wards of Light</em> might just be their best album yet.</p><p></p>
<!--kg-card-begin: html-->
<iframe style="border: 0; width: 100%; height: 120px;" src="https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/album=2390211692/size=large/bgcol=333333/linkcol=e99708/tracklist=false/artwork=small/transparent=true/" seamless><a href="https://dreadnoughtdenver.bandcamp.com/album/wars-of-spirit-wards-of-light?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Wars of Spirit // Wards of Light by Dreadnought</a></iframe>
