";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}}}i:9;a:6:{s:4:"data";s:0:"";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";s:5:"child";a:4:{s:0:"";a:6:{s:5:"title";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:51:"Track Premiere: Set Your Ears Ablaze with Convulsif";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:11:"description";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:121:"Swiss experimental rock band Convulsif unleashes a bass-heavy burst of groove and noise from their upcoming fourth album ";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"link";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:95:"https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/08/29/track-premiere-set-your-ears-ablaze-with-convulsif/";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"guid";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:24:"6a92df6d321ef100015dd3d4";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:1:{s:11:"isPermaLink";s:5:"false";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:8:"category";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:9:"Premieres";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:17:"experimental rock";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:7:"pubDate";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:29:"Sat, 29 Aug 2026 13:39:39 GMT";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:32:"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/";a:1:{s:7:"creator";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:14:"Bridget Hughes";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:29:"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/";a:1:{s:7:"content";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:0:"";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:2:{s:3:"url";s:106:"https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/08/IMG_0379.jpeg";s:6:"medium";s:5:"image";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:40:"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/";a:1:{s:7:"encoded";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:2299:"<img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/08/IMG_0379.jpeg" alt="Track Premiere: Set Your Ears Ablaze with Convulsif"><p>After the brutal heatwaves of August, the chilly depths of winter feel like a distant threat. But signs of the creeping cold are slowly emerging; cooling nights, the return of pumpkin spice, a dwindling tomato season. For those ready for the crisp return of colder weather, there&#x2019;s <strong>Convulsif</strong>&#x2019;s latest album, which is slowly unfolding like the change of seasons. Today, a new glimpse is unveiled.&#xA0;</p><p>Fittingly, &#x201C;A Torch Then Blaze&#x201D; is something of a transitional track on <em>Anatomy of Rage</em>. A quick, bass-heavy interlude that emerges with sinister intent and lurching grooves spliced with grinding noise that connects the blistering first chapter with the funeral pyres of the middle tracks.</p><p>While short, &#x201C;A Torch Then Blaze&#x201D; illustrates the fascinating juxtapositions created by Convulsif: maximalist experiments constrained within minimalist production, chaotic noise rock sharpened to a razor&#x2019;s edge. Rather than embrace the massive production often found in experimental rock, Convulsif keeps their sound centered and brutally direct. Structure loses all meaning - songs range from 76 seconds to nearly 20 minutes - allowing tightly coiled grooves and jagged, jazzy rhythms to take control. The clarity creates a menacing beast of noise and abrasion, one that&#x2019;s encapsulated by the brief warning siren of &#x201C;A Torch Then Blaze&#x201D; as it groans and explodes into noisy flames.&#xA0;</p><p><em>Anatomy of Rage</em> will be released on October 1, 2026. <a href="https://convulsif.bandcamp.com/album/anatomy-of-rage?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com"><u>Pre-order</u></a> on Bandcamp and follow the band via their <a href="http://www.convulsif.ch/?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com"><u>website</u></a>.&#xA0;</p><figure class="kg-card kg-embed-card"><iframe width="100%" height="400" scrolling="no" frameborder="no" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media" src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?visual=true&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F2197047083&amp;show_artwork=true&amp;secret_token=s-pIpIu3uFAok"></iframe></figure>";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}}}i:10;a:6:{s:4:"data";s:0:"";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";s:5:"child";a:4:{s:0:"";a:6:{s:5:"title";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:66:"EXCLUSIVE PREMIERE: Pelegrin Wander Into &quot;Sun And Blood&quot;";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:11:"description";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:189:"It's been a while since we've visited with one of my favorite "microscenes" - the French stoner and doom metal scene. Luckily, one of my favorite bands from that area of the world are back!";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"link";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:98:"https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/08/28/exclusive-premiere-pelegrin-wander-into-sun-and-blood/";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"guid";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:24:"6a91906c321ef100015dd1f8";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:1:{s:11:"isPermaLink";s:5:"false";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:8:"category";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:9:"Premieres";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:8:"Pelegrin";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:7:"pubDate";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:29:"Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:00:04 GMT";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:32:"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/";a:1:{s:7:"creator";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:15:"Eden Kupermintz";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:29:"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/";a:1:{s:7:"content";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:0:"";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:2:{s:3:"url";s:106:"https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/08/unnamed-1.jpg";s:6:"medium";s:5:"image";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:40:"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/";a:1:{s:7:"encoded";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:2537:"<img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/08/unnamed-1.jpg" alt="EXCLUSIVE PREMIERE: Pelegrin Wander Into &quot;Sun And Blood&quot;"><p>It&apos;s been a while since we&apos;ve visited with one of my favorite &quot;microscenes&quot; - the French stoner and doom metal scene. Luckily, one of my favorite bands from that area of the world are back with a new album this year and have graciously afforded me the privilege of premiering a single from said album. I covered <strong>Pelegrin</strong> for <a href="https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2023/02/16/pelegrin-premiere/" rel="noreferrer">the first time four years ago</a> with another premiere and I&apos;ve been waiting for more music since then. Happily, &quot;Sun and Blood&quot; does not disappoint with a trippy, occult-steeped video and, more importantly, a more muscular and present approach to Pelegrin&apos;s sound than before. Head on down below to take the journey!</p><figure class="kg-card kg-embed-card"><iframe width="200" height="113" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/GHwN7xrU7sg?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen title="Pelegrin - &quot;Sun and Blood&quot; (Official Music Video) | Ripple Music - 2026"></iframe></figure><p>Pelegrin&apos;s previous music can be described as &quot;airy&quot;, a certain thinness which worked very well with the expansive can of psychedelia they were going for. But here, the adjective would be &quot;earthy&quot; - the main riff is much more present in the mix, its tone thicker and heavier. The drums are punctual like falling stones, lending the track momentum and groove. Sprinkle in the same excellent vocals from the previous release, one scorching, desert-sun hot solo, and a few more touches here and there from excellent backing riffs and thick bass, and you&apos;ve got yourself a treat. I also love the lighter guitars which open the track, setting the ground for the shimmering, stoner sound the band is so good for.</p><p>&quot;Sun and Blood&quot; comes to us from the upcoming <em>The Curse of Nephtar</em>, due to release on September 4th on the mighty Ripple Music. <a href="https://pelegrinmusic.bandcamp.com/album/the-curse-of-nephtar?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com" rel="noreferrer">You can head on over here to pre-order it</a> (and also check out that <em>glorious</em> art work in full).</p>";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}}}i:11;a:6:{s:4:"data";s:0:"";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";s:5:"child";a:4:{s:0:"";a:6:{s:5:"title";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:24:"Release Roundup: 8/28/26";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:11:"description";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:292:"It's a big one, featuring new releases from Mastodon, Perpetual Paradox, Gorod, Russian Circles, Dinosaur Jr, Flotsam and Jetsam, Kanmelot, Airbourne, Exumer, Dreamwell, Ninth Realm, Squid Pisser, Triosphere, Sev Lezu, Besvarjelsen, Carceral, Black Spikes, In This Moment, Turnstile and more!";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"link";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:68:"https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/08/28/release-roundup-8-28-26/";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"guid";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:24:"6a8e479c2dd4b30001d53990";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:1:{s:11:"isPermaLink";s:5:"false";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:8:"category";a:4:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:19:"Release Day Roundup";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:8:"Mastodon";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}i:2;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:17:"Perpetual Paradox";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}i:3;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:5:"gorod";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:7:"pubDate";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:29:"Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:00:13 GMT";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:32:"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/";a:1:{s:7:"creator";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:14:"Joshua Bulleid";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:29:"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/";a:1:{s:7:"content";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:0:"";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:2:{s:3:"url";s:125:"https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/08/Gorod-The-Ember-Gone-768x768.jpg";s:6:"medium";s:5:"image";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:40:"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/";a:1:{s:7:"encoded";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:23195:"<h2 id="top-picks">Top Picks&#xA0;</h2><img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/08/Gorod-The-Ember-Gone-768x768.jpg" alt="Release Roundup: 8/28/26"><p>There are more good and interesting albums out this week than there have been all month!</p><h3 id="mastodon-%E2%80%93-marrow-deep-prog-metal">Mastodon &#x2013; <em>Marrow Deep</em> (prog metal) </h3>
<!--kg-card-begin: html-->
<iframe style="border: 0; width: 100%; height: 120px;" src="https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/album=3653801622/size=large/bgcol=333333/linkcol=e99708/tracklist=false/artwork=small/transparent=true/" seamless><a href="https://mastodon.bandcamp.com/album/marrow-deep?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Marrow Deep by Mastodon</a></iframe>
<!--kg-card-end: html-->
<p>From my <a href="https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/08/28/mastodon-marrow-deep/" rel="noreferrer">review</a>:</p><p>&quot;Whatever you think of the albums in between, it&apos;s hard to deny that <em>Marrow Deep </em>is the best <strong>Mastodon </strong>album since <em>Once More &apos;round the Sun </em>(2014)&#x2014;or even longer, for (silly) people who don&apos;t like that album for whatever reason. The record continuously conjures up the Mastodonian triumphs of their past, with its overall sonic palette and songwriting sensibilities are something of a mix between what are perhaps the band&apos;s two greatest triumphs in <em>Blood Mountain </em>(2006) and <em>Crack the Skye </em>(2009). Even then though, it sounds less like a rehash or a missing link than something like what <em>Emperor of Sand</em> (2017) could and maybe should have been, in its masterful blend of classic and continuous Mastodon sounds.&quot;</p><h3 id="perpetual-paradox-%E2%80%93-may-misery-befall-you-thrashy-tech-deathcore">Perpetual Paradox &#x2013; <em>May Misery Befall You</em> (thrashy tech-death/core) </h3><h3 id></h3><p>From my <a href="https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/08/26/the-anatomy-of-perpetual-paradox/" rel="noreferrer">Anatomy Of</a> post:</p><p>&quot;You might not have heard of London&apos;s <strong>Perpetual Paradox</strong>, but you should definitely give them a listen. Although ostensibly a groove-laden death-thrash/core outfit, there&apos;s a lot more going on here than that already enticing description might suggest. The 5 tracks on their new EP <em>May Misery Befall You </em>deliver a killer combination of wiry, off-kilter lead-work that reminds me of <strong>Psycroptic</strong> (except without the <a href="https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/07/17/release-roundup-7-17-26/" rel="noreferrer">Nazi merch</a>), along with some added progressiveness &#xE0; la <strong>Rivers of Nihil</strong>, the crunch of <strong>Lamb of God </strong>and brutality of <strong>Fit for an Autopsy</strong>. It&apos;s a potent concoction to be sure and one of the more exciting &quot;new&quot; artists I&apos;ve come across this year.&quot;</p><figure class="kg-card kg-embed-card"><iframe width="200" height="113" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/oxdTp4F7yWc?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen title="Perpetual Paradox - Source Of Hate"></iframe></figure><h3 id="gorod-%E2%80%93-the-ember-gone-progressive-tech-death">Gorod &#x2013; <em>The Ember Gone</em> (progressive tech-death) </h3><h3 id="-1"></h3><p>This new <strong>Gorod</strong> album is also very good, and also a lot better than the last one(and also also kind of a mix of the two albums discussed above?).</p><figure class="kg-card kg-embed-card"><iframe width="200" height="113" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/qNaFD-n7E5c?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen title="GOROD | Remains [Official Visualizer]"></iframe></figure><h2 id="release-roundup">Release Roundup</h2><h3 id="airbourne-%E2%80%93-airbourne-ac-dc">Airbourne &#x2013; <em>Airbourne</em> (AC, DC) </h3><figure class="kg-card kg-embed-card"><iframe width="200" height="113" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/6IMg6TRZK-k?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen title="Airbourne - Alive After Death (Last Plane Out)"></iframe></figure><p>Angoixa &#x2013; <a href="https://angoixadeathmetal.bandcamp.com/album/vida-i-mort?from=search&amp;search_item_id=2928760672&amp;search_item_type=a&amp;search_match_part=%3F&amp;search_page_id=5687989856&amp;search_page_no=1&amp;search_rank=1&amp;search_sig=3832bbb22cdc308df211908f193577d9&amp;ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Vida i Mort</a> (death metal)</p><p><a>Azgaal &#x2013; </a><a href="https://fetznerdeathrecords.bandcamp.com/album/azgaal-divine-hitman?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Divine Hitman</a> (black metal)</p><p><a>Beseech &#x2013; </a><a href="https://beseech.bandcamp.com/album/future-present-past?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Future. Present. Past</a> (melogoth)</p><p>Black Door &#x2013; <a href="https://chronosdefied.bandcamp.com/album/in-the-shadows-of-a-funerary-gleam?from=search&amp;search_item_id=2453497501&amp;search_item_type=a&amp;search_match_part=%3F&amp;search_page_id=5687989492&amp;search_page_no=1&amp;search_rank=1&amp;search_sig=1a9fbf03599256ada991ed6857443f50&amp;ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">In the Shadows of a Funerary Gleam</a> (black metal)</p><p>Beartooth &#x2013; <a href="https://beartooth.bandcamp.com/album/pure-ecstasy?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com" rel="noreferrer">Pure Ecstasy</a> (y tho?) </p><h3 id="besvarjelsen-%E2%80%93-till-gl%C3%B6mskan-ad-oblivionem-stoner-prog">Besvarjelsen &#x2013; <em>Till Gl&#xF6;mskan Ad Oblivionem</em> (stoner prog) </h3>
<!--kg-card-begin: html-->
<iframe style="border: 0; width: 100%; height: 120px;" src="https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/album=525249269/size=large/bgcol=333333/linkcol=e99708/tracklist=false/artwork=small/transparent=true/" seamless><a href="https://besvarjelsen.bandcamp.com/album/till-gl-mskan-ad-oblivionem?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Till Gl&#xF6;mskan Ad Oblivionem by Besv&#xE4;rjelsen</a></iframe>
<!--kg-card-end: html-->
<h3 id="black-spikes-%E2%80%93-ydos-progressiveblackened-baddiecore">Black Spikes &#x2013; <em>Ydos</em> (progressive/blackened baddiecore?) </h3>
<!--kg-card-begin: html-->
<iframe style="border: 0; width: 100%; height: 120px;" src="https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/album=858202532/size=large/bgcol=333333/linkcol=e99708/tracklist=false/artwork=small/transparent=true/" seamless><a href="https://blackspikes.bandcamp.com/album/ydos?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Ydos by Black Spikes</a></iframe>
